    """
    The event that starts the workflow; `condition` decides whether that occurrence runs it. `conversation_opened` runs when a conversation opens; `first_message_received` when the contact writes first in a conversation, before any message from the business; `message_received` on every incoming message; `message_sent` within 15 minutes of an outgoing message, unless the contact replied first; `conversation_inactive` and `team_message_unanswered` after `inactivity_seconds`. `schedule` runs at each of its `schedule.times` on each conversation assigned then to a member its `condition` names with `assignee` `is`, which it requires. `conversation_assigned` runs when a conversation is assigned to a member; the assignment an AI handoff makes does not run it. Both take only `turn_on_ai`, `turn_off_ai`, `decision` and `end` steps, and only they take `turn_on_ai` and `turn_off_ai`. `call_received` decides who answers a WhatsApp call on the WhatsApp numbers with AI calls on that its `condition` names: its flow takes only `answer_call`, `decline_call` and `decision`s on `channel` and `time`, and the first active one that reaches a call step, in most recently published order, decides, over whoever holds the conversation. `at_time` is deprecated: read as `schedule`.
    """
    condition: Optional[Union[ConditionInput, Union[CreateWorkflowDefinitionCondition, CreateWorkflowDefinitionCondition1]]]
